WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.556 --> 00:00:12.956
Listen, I'm British-born
and by a Nigerian raised.

00:00:12.996 --> 00:00:15.676
There were expectations,

00:00:15.716 --> 00:00:17.636
different ways I was supposed to go.

00:00:17.636 --> 00:00:19.356
My career options for one,

00:00:19.356 --> 00:00:21.756
some of you may already know.

00:00:21.796 --> 00:00:24.956
As an African, you get three choices.

00:00:24.996 --> 00:00:27.156
Please, repeat after me.

00:00:27.516 --> 00:00:30.636
You are going to be a doctor --

00:00:30.676 --> 00:00:31.876
Audience: A doctor.

00:00:31.876 --> 00:00:33.036
FB: A lawyer.

00:00:33.076 --> 00:00:34.236
Audience: A lawyer.

00:00:34.276 --> 00:00:36.316
FB: Or a business man.

00:00:36.316 --> 00:00:38.236
Audience: Or a businessman.

00:00:38.276 --> 00:00:41.156
FB: Now, I did a thing
that brought on quite a bit of stress.

00:00:41.156 --> 00:00:44.116
That was me saying, "Mum,
babes, I did my best,

00:00:44.156 --> 00:00:46.516
but that's not how I'm going to go.

00:00:46.956 --> 00:00:48.916
I'm going to be an actor."

00:00:50.036 --> 00:00:52.796
"Why do you want to prostitute
your emotions for money?"

00:00:53.756 --> 00:00:54.916
Was my mum's reaction.

00:00:54.956 --> 00:00:57.236
Now, in all fairness,

00:00:57.276 --> 00:01:00.676
what I was asking for
was this complete abstraction.

00:01:01.116 --> 00:01:04.276
But the more I succeeded,
the more my mum could see, right?

00:01:04.316 --> 00:01:09.516
Her idea of what was possible
was being reimagined

00:01:09.556 --> 00:01:10.916
with me.

00:01:10.956 --> 00:01:12.796
I was the lead on the West End.

00:01:13.196 --> 00:01:19.076
I was about to be a part, a small part,
a walk-on part in a massive film.

00:01:19.116 --> 00:01:22.676
I'm building my career and then boom.

00:01:24.516 --> 00:01:30.076
I’m falling apart, and it seems
I am dealing with climate anxiety.

00:01:32.116 --> 00:01:37.116
Building my dream and watching the world
literally burn in front of me

00:01:37.116 --> 00:01:39.196
and very little being done.

00:01:40.276 --> 00:01:41.436
I'm panicking.

00:01:41.796 --> 00:01:43.236
Frozen like a mannequin.

00:01:43.276 --> 00:01:45.636
Until I see environmental
activism happening,

00:01:45.676 --> 00:01:47.236
and I jump in.

00:01:47.276 --> 00:01:49.796
But whilst on the protests
and in the meeting rooms,

00:01:49.836 --> 00:01:51.876
a question takes over me.

00:01:52.916 --> 00:01:54.796
Why don't these people look like me?

00:01:55.796 --> 00:01:57.996
Why is it when I think
about climate activism,

00:01:58.036 --> 00:02:00.596
I think about white middle-class people?

00:02:00.596 --> 00:02:02.316
Is it a white middle-class problem?

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:07.836
A crisis that seems to require more
time, effort, money, work to do

00:02:07.876 --> 00:02:09.436
or know anything about

00:02:09.476 --> 00:02:11.876
and I'm talking about those
that have the privilege

00:02:11.876 --> 00:02:14.276
to think about anything else but survival.

00:02:15.276 --> 00:02:18.116
It feels like people of color
experience barriers

00:02:18.156 --> 00:02:20.316
towards the forefront
of the climate movement,

00:02:20.356 --> 00:02:26.316
and it seems that the reasons lie behind
our underlining principles of survival.

00:02:27.516 --> 00:02:29.076
To keep your head down.

00:02:29.596 --> 00:02:34.516
Do your work, and don’t get into trouble.

00:02:35.316 --> 00:02:37.956
Survive, and dare to thrive.

00:02:37.996 --> 00:02:40.756
Protest, yeah, but only
for imminent survival.

00:02:40.796 --> 00:02:43.716
See, we've got family
that's been in this country for 40 years

00:02:43.716 --> 00:02:45.396
and still feel like new arrivals.

00:02:45.396 --> 00:02:48.796
And we have a history
of disappearing in the night.

00:02:49.196 --> 00:02:51.756
Shipped off to someplace or just mourned.

00:02:52.556 --> 00:02:54.316
No room for the eco fight.

00:02:55.116 --> 00:02:56.876
I mean, me Fehinti Balogun,

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:59.196
on this stage right now doing a TED Talk,

00:02:59.196 --> 00:03:02.876
I am about four times more likely

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.076
to have force used against me
if I'm arrested

00:03:05.116 --> 00:03:06.516
than my white counterpart.

00:03:06.996 --> 00:03:10.876
I’m about seven times more likely
to be stopped and searched.

00:03:10.876 --> 00:03:13.956
And with a new policing bill
and public order bill,

00:03:13.996 --> 00:03:15.996
these biases are only set to increase.

00:03:16.476 --> 00:03:18.756
Noise restriction on protests.

00:03:18.796 --> 00:03:21.436
Criminalization of protesters

00:03:21.436 --> 00:03:24.396
without having to convict them of a crime.

00:03:24.436 --> 00:03:26.036
Police can stop and search anyone

00:03:26.076 --> 00:03:29.036
saying they have reasonable suspicion

00:03:29.076 --> 00:03:31.796
and threaten peaceful protest tactics.

00:03:31.836 --> 00:03:33.316
The fear is real.

00:03:34.596 --> 00:03:35.756
So, you know.

00:03:36.636 --> 00:03:37.996
Keep your head down.

00:03:38.756 --> 00:03:39.916
Do your work.

00:03:40.476 --> 00:03:43.316
And don't get into trouble.

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:46.076
Get yourself a piece of the pie, right?

00:03:46.076 --> 00:03:50.756
But that suggests the payoff
will be in a world

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:53.076
similar to the ones
our parents grew up in.

00:03:54.076 --> 00:03:55.956
London was hot, boy.

00:03:55.956 --> 00:03:57.676
Forty degrees,

00:03:57.716 --> 00:04:00.036
one of the hottest summers in history

00:04:00.076 --> 00:04:04.596
after one of the hottest
summers in history.

00:04:04.596 --> 00:04:06.556
Some people couldn’t go outside.

00:04:06.596 --> 00:04:09.116
Plants were either dried up or on fire.

00:04:09.156 --> 00:04:12.396
Countries were either
underwater or on fire.

00:04:12.436 --> 00:04:15.476
This extreme weather
is only set to increase.

00:04:15.516 --> 00:04:18.596
If crops die, well, that makes
food more expensive,

00:04:18.636 --> 00:04:23.076
affecting working class communities,
communities of color first.

00:04:23.076 --> 00:04:26.996
That world that they grew up in is gone.

00:04:28.796 --> 00:04:31.276
But what if, and go with me on this,

00:04:31.316 --> 00:04:37.276
what if climate change is just
a symptom of a bigger problem?

00:04:38.156 --> 00:04:40.276
And what if it is the same problem

00:04:40.316 --> 00:04:43.916
that causes racism and sexism and ableism?

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.716
What if all of these things
are just symptoms

00:04:46.756 --> 00:04:48.916
of a bigger problem?

00:04:49.356 --> 00:04:50.516
Ready?

00:04:51.476 --> 00:04:55.676
White supremacist patriarchal capitalism.

00:04:57.916 --> 00:05:01.996
(Applause)

00:05:02.036 --> 00:05:06.116
It feels scary
because it feels like a concept,

00:05:06.156 --> 00:05:08.836
even though our society
is quite literally based on it.

00:05:08.876 --> 00:05:10.596
Infinite growth

00:05:10.636 --> 00:05:14.196
with finite resources
at whatever the cost.

00:05:14.916 --> 00:05:16.836
Those forms of oppression wouldn't exist

00:05:16.876 --> 00:05:19.196
if it didn't make someone money.

00:05:19.716 --> 00:05:21.676
I mean, in the UK.

00:05:21.676 --> 00:05:25.196
slavery plantations in the Caribbean
provided the raw materials

00:05:25.236 --> 00:05:27.876
needed for industrial change and growth

00:05:27.876 --> 00:05:29.836
in the British Empire, money.

00:05:29.836 --> 00:05:33.316
Not to mention the genocides
and the conquests, more money.

00:05:33.316 --> 00:05:35.676
The liberation of oil by liberators,

00:05:35.676 --> 00:05:39.436
that deliberate the price
of liberation whilst polluting soil.

00:05:39.436 --> 00:05:40.996
Get that money.

00:05:41.036 --> 00:05:44.156
Shout out to Shell, by the way,

00:05:44.156 --> 00:05:47.916
who historically have taken oil
from my country of origin, Nigeria.

00:05:47.916 --> 00:05:52.276
Nigeria, who pollutes almost ten
times less than England.

00:05:52.316 --> 00:05:55.076
As do so many colonized countries,
and you know what?

00:05:55.556 --> 00:05:57.636
It seems to me

00:05:57.676 --> 00:06:00.476
that some of the people
who are the most affected

00:06:00.516 --> 00:06:01.956
pollute the least.

00:06:02.716 --> 00:06:05.756
The ones who have been
historically stolen from.

00:06:06.916 --> 00:06:09.956
Climate change is modern colonialism.

00:06:11.156 --> 00:06:15.076
So we know, with all of this,
with a colonial mindset,

00:06:15.116 --> 00:06:17.076
with a capitalist mindset

00:06:17.116 --> 00:06:19.836
that even if we have a magical technology

00:06:19.836 --> 00:06:22.676
that clears the air
and makes everything safe,

00:06:22.716 --> 00:06:25.476
it would only operate
in certain neighborhoods.

00:06:25.476 --> 00:06:27.596
We’re dealing with structure.

00:06:28.996 --> 00:06:33.076
A structure that told me
to keep my head down.

00:06:33.556 --> 00:06:35.476
A structure and a media

00:06:35.516 --> 00:06:40.316
that chose to omit that six percent
of the population, Indigenous people,

00:06:40.316 --> 00:06:43.916
protect 80 percent
of the world's biodiversity.

00:06:44.476 --> 00:06:48.956
Chose to omit that one of the most
important climate protests in history

00:06:48.996 --> 00:06:50.556
was led by a Nigerian,

00:06:50.596 --> 00:06:53.476
Ken Saro-Wiwa of the Ogoni people.

00:06:53.476 --> 00:06:57.436
Chose to omit the effectiveness
of grassroots movements

00:06:57.476 --> 00:06:58.916
and community action.

00:06:58.916 --> 00:07:01.196
People like BEN
and Wretched of the Earth

00:07:01.236 --> 00:07:03.516
May Garden Projects, to name a few.

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:07.556
Chose to omit the UK's
constant investment in fossil fuels

00:07:07.596 --> 00:07:11.196
takes away from any aid it wants to send
to countries like Pakistan

00:07:11.236 --> 00:07:15.676
but then reminds me I should recycle more.

00:07:17.796 --> 00:07:20.356
If it is that structure that tells me

00:07:20.396 --> 00:07:23.796
it is about my own
individual purpose and guilt,

00:07:23.796 --> 00:07:27.996
maybe it's worthless,
I feel the power is in the masses.

00:07:28.836 --> 00:07:30.356
So I joined groups.

00:07:30.756 --> 00:07:34.436
Local and in my job like cooking.

00:07:34.476 --> 00:07:36.516
With all my different hobs.

00:07:36.556 --> 00:07:39.156
One being Equity for a Green New Deal.

00:07:39.516 --> 00:07:42.756
Pension divestment,
putting pressure on heels.

00:07:43.076 --> 00:07:45.876
Then I took lessons from Copwatch UK.

00:07:45.876 --> 00:07:48.716
Taught me my rights with police
arrests and interventions,

00:07:48.716 --> 00:07:50.836
discerning their intentions.

00:07:50.876 --> 00:07:54.396
I learned I have to think radically now.

00:07:55.476 --> 00:07:56.676
About strategy.

00:07:58.556 --> 00:08:00.076
And kindness.

00:08:01.116 --> 00:08:03.236
Kindness for myself

00:08:03.276 --> 00:08:05.076
and those right behind us.

00:08:05.156 --> 00:08:08.476
To be held by them and to hold right back.

00:08:08.516 --> 00:08:12.316
Well, that’s community, right
there is strategy in that.

00:08:13.716 --> 00:08:14.876
Then what's my capacity?

00:08:14.916 --> 00:08:16.076
How much can I give?

00:08:16.116 --> 00:08:19.036
Because I got rent, auditions,
I've got to live.

00:08:19.076 --> 00:08:22.396
And when I have my capacity,
I think, well, what's my aim?

00:08:22.676 --> 00:08:25.636
Where am I helpful?
How do I give weight to my claims?

00:08:25.636 --> 00:08:27.636
It's about strategy, right?

00:08:27.676 --> 00:08:29.796
So why integrate?

00:08:29.836 --> 00:08:34.116
Well, I speak to ignite,
connect and always agitate.

00:08:34.116 --> 00:08:35.316
Let's go back.

00:08:35.316 --> 00:08:37.396
Because this is important, agitate.

00:08:38.636 --> 00:08:43.156
Call out inaction,
point to solution, tell the truth.

00:08:43.196 --> 00:08:46.156
Get all that money out of fossil fuels,

00:08:46.196 --> 00:08:47.996
pension investments, accounts,

00:08:48.036 --> 00:08:52.436
hand over power,
make them want to be radical.

00:08:52.476 --> 00:08:54.076
Connect.

00:08:54.116 --> 00:08:56.116
There are people in spaces just like this

00:08:56.156 --> 00:08:58.836
that need to be connected
to grassroots movements,

00:08:58.836 --> 00:09:02.156
who need the attention,
the space, the funding,

00:09:02.196 --> 00:09:05.196
and they need you.

00:09:07.596 --> 00:09:08.876
Ignite.

00:09:09.196 --> 00:09:13.796
Remind everybody watching
that you are not powerless.

00:09:14.116 --> 00:09:16.316
That, "Ah man, there's nothing we can do,

00:09:16.316 --> 00:09:17.476
just keep going."

00:09:17.516 --> 00:09:19.716
is a symptom,

00:09:19.716 --> 00:09:20.876
not cure.

00:09:21.796 --> 00:09:25.756
That you stand on years
worth of resistance and success,

00:09:25.756 --> 00:09:27.396
that you are needed.

00:09:28.316 --> 00:09:31.596
That you, just like my mum,

00:09:31.596 --> 00:09:35.116
have the power to reimagine

00:09:35.156 --> 00:09:36.796
what you think is possible.

00:09:37.876 --> 00:09:39.156
So now we speak.

00:09:39.916 --> 00:09:41.876
We strategize.

00:09:41.916 --> 00:09:45.916
And we think: How does this
action aid the next step?

00:09:47.636 --> 00:09:48.796
Thank you.

00:09:48.836 --> 00:09:55.156
(Applause and cheers)

